.SH NAME
LD860 - Link editor for iPSC\*R/860\fR\fR\fR\fR\& object files. 
.\" End Summary
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
\&\fBld860\fR\fR\& [ \fR\fIoptions\fI\fR\& ] \fR\fIfilename\fI\fR\
\& ... 
.SH ARGUMENTS 
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fR\fIfilename\fI\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' The name of the iPSC/860\& object file or library. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.LP
You may specify the following \fR\fIoptions\fI\fR\& in any order:
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-o\fR\fR\& \fR\fIobjfile\fI\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Put the output object file in \fR\fI\
objfile\fI\fR\&. If this option is not specified, the default object \
file name is \fR\fIa.out\fI\fR\&. If a file with the same name already exists, it is deleted.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-e\fR\fR\& \fR\fIsymbol\fI\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Specify \fR\fI\
symbol\fI\fR\& as the entry-point. The default entry-point is \fR\fR\
\&_\|\&_start\fR\fR\&. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-v\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Ignored. Accepted for backwards compatibility.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-y\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Ignored. Accepted for backwards compatibility.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-contig\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Force \fB\&.text\fR\fR\& and \fB\
\&.data\fR\fR\& sections from adjacent modules to be contiguous when \
combined, instead of aligning \fB\&.text\fR\fR\& sections on 32-byte boundaries, and \fB\
\&.data\fR\fR\& sections are aligned on 16-byte boundaries. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-intel\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Use Intel specified relocation types for COFF.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-aix\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Use Intel-specified relocation types for COFF.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-T\fR\fR\& \fR\fIinteger\fI\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Specify the address at which the \fB\
\&.text\fR\fR\& section is to be loaded. The default is \&0xF0400000.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-D\fR\fR\& \fR\fIinteger\fI\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Specify the length of the \fB\
\&.data\fR\fR\& section to be \fR\fIinteger\fI\fR\& bytes. The \fB\
\&.data\fR\fR\& section is padded with zero to the specified length, which may not be less than the summed \
length derived from the object modules.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-d\fR\fR\& \fR\fIinteger\fI\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Specify the address at which the \fB\
\&.data\fR\fR\& section is to be loaded. The default is \&0x1000.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-u\fR\fR\& \fR\fIsymbol\fI\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Initialize the symbol table with \fR\fI\
symbol\fI\fR\&. The linker considers \fR\fIsymbol\fI\fR\& to be \
undefined.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-t\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Display the name of each object file or library as it is processed.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-M\fR\fR\&,\fB\&-Mx\fR\fR\&,\fB\&-Mw\fR\fR\&,\fB\&-Mxw
.br
\fR\fRIgnored. Accepted for backwards compatibility.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-m\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Ignored. Accepted for backwards compatibility.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-s\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Strip all symbols from the output object file.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-r\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Retain relocation entries in the output object file, to allow incremental linking. \
The output object file produced with \fB\&-r\fR\fR\& can be used as an input object file in \
another link. When \fB\&-r\fR\fR\& is used, \fB\&-o\fR\fR\& must also be specified.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-B\fR\fR\& \fR\fIinteger\fI\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Specifies the address to use for the base of the \fB\
\&.bss\fR\fR\& section for all following object modules. This option may be used multiple times, and affects only objects that \
appear after the option in the command line.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-p\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Align the \fB\&.data\fR\fR\& section of the following module on a page boundary. This option \
may be repeated as necessary, and applies only to the next object file.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-k\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Start the \fB\&.text\fR\fR\& and \fB\
\&.data\fR\fR\& sections exactly at the addresses specified by the \fB\
\&-T\fR\fR\& and \fB\&-d\fR\fR\& options (or at the defaults if the options are not given) without performing the \
normal modifications to those addresses to make the file pageable.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-i386\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Put the magic number for Intel386\*(tM\fR\fR\fR\fR\
\& COFF files in the output file, instead of the magic number for i860\*(tM\fR\fR\fR\fR\
\& COFF files.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-quiet\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Ignored. Accepted for backwards compatibility.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-dos\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Linker is being used on an MS-DOS system.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-f\fR\fR\& \fR\fIfilelist\fI\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Read in a list of files to be linked from file \fR\fI\
filelist\fI\fR\&. Names in the file can be separated by a comma, a space, a tab, or a linefeed. This option may be used \
multiple times.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-be\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Process all data defined in \fB\
\&.data\fR\fR\& sections as ``big-endian'' data (high-order byte \
first). Forces the \fB\&-bess\fR\fR\& option, as well.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-bess\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' COFF headers and control structures are written ``big-endian.''
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-qa\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Set COFF timestamp to 0.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
Use\fB\& ld860\fR\fR\& to link-edit the named file(s). 
.LP
Object files and libraries are processed in the order specified.
.LP
Libraries are searched for unsatisfied externals when they are processed, and are not reopened to \
satisfy any symbols that might not have been satisfied.
.LP
The \fB\&-r\fR\fR\& option requires the \fB\&-o\fR\fR\& option.
.LP
If the \fB\&-r\fR\fR\& and the \fB\&-s\fR\fR\& options are used together, the \fB\
\&-s\fR\fR\& option is ignored.
.LP
If the \fB\&-r\fR\fR\& and the \fB\&-e\fR\fR\& options are used together, the \fB\
\&-e\fR\fR\& option is ignored.
.LP
If the \fB\&-f\fR\fR\& option is used, the \fB\&-B\fR\fR\& and \fB\
\&-p\fR\fR\& options are applied as if the object file names appeared in place \
of the \fB\&-f\fR\fR\& option.
.LP
The default \fR\fIcrt0.o\fI\fR\& (the initial object file) has \fR\fR\
ld$start\fR\fR\& as its entry point, and the compiler drivers \
\&(\fBicc\fR\fR\& and \fBif77\fR\fR\&) always use \fR\fR\&-e ld$start\fR\fR\
\& in the command lines they synthesize for \fBld860\fR\fR\&.
.LP
The compiler drivers always override the beginning address of the \fB\
\&.text\fR\fR\& section to be 0 by putting \fR\fR\&-T 0x0\fR\fR\
\& in the synthesized command line.
.LP
The compiler drivers always override the beginning address of the \fB\
\&.data\fR\fR\& section to be 0x10000000 by putting \fR\fR\&-d 0x10000000\fR\fR\
\& in the synthesized command line.
.SH SEE ALSO
